      "The Tenant of Wildfell Hall arrived in 1848 under the name Acton Bell. Its author, Anne Brontë, had written a novel in which an unhappy marriage, addiction and a woman's attempts to protect herself became central subjects. Readers could confront those subjects without first knowing that a young woman from a Yorkshire parsonage had written them.",
