      "For much of her reign, Elizabeth I was asked a question whose answer would alter the political future of England: who would follow her on the throne? She did not provide the public, formal designation many councillors and parliamentarians wanted. A monarch who could issue proclamations, command government and negotiate with foreign rulers withheld one particular kind of announcement.",
      "Elizabeth inherited the throne in 1558 after years in which England had seen disputed successions, religious reversals and the consequences of dynastic uncertainty. Her own position had once been precarious. Questions of marriage and heirs carried implications for relations with Catholic and Protestant powers, the nobility and the future of the Tudor dynasty.",
