      "Victoria ruled Britain from 1837 to 1901, in an age of expanding newspapers, imperial power and intense interest in royal domestic life. The monarch's family appeared in public imagery as a model of respectability. Private remarks, however, were not necessarily intended for the same audience as speeches and official statements.",
