      "When Thomas Hardy died in 1928, future readers inherited a remarkable literary career—and a record of his life that the writer had already worked to shape. Letters, notebooks and other personal papers had been destroyed; a biographical account prepared with Hardy's involvement would appear under the name of his widow, Florence.",
      "Hardy grew up in Dorset and became internationally known as a novelist and poet. His fiction often investigated social convention, desire, class and the power of institutions over individuals. Public responses to books such as Jude the Obscure were sometimes hostile, and after the 1890s he concentrated chiefly on poetry.",
